name mig29-gun-1
timeout 120

# THE GSh-301 — a 30 mm gun on the same generic apparatus the M61A1 uses, and what the file measures is
# whether the KINETIC path carries a different calibre without a new constant.
#
#   core/FBGun.h   M61A1     1,030 m/s   6,000 rd/min   510 rounds   0.100 kg   sigma 2.23 mrad
#                  GSh-301     860 m/s   1,500 rd/min   150 rounds   0.390 kg   sigma 6.0  mrad
#   [DER, doc/modules/mig29/weapons.md §4.4] per round the Soviet gun carries 2.7x the energy
#   (144.2 kJ against 53 kJ) and delivers 0.68x the energy flux; its drum lasts 6.0 s against 5.1 s.
#   Against core/FBGunBallistics' density model that is FEWER, HEAVIER impacts in a WIDER cone — and the
#   wider cone is why the documented effective range (800 m) is SHORTER despite the higher muzzle
#   energy. Nothing in core/FBDamageModel was touched for it: the J/m^2 currency carries both.
#
# WHY THIS IS A BRIEFED BURST AND NOT A DOGFIGHT. `gun-bfm.fbm` measures the F-16's gun by WINNING a
# tracking pass, which measures the pilot and the weapon together. On this airframe that is not
# available yet and the reason is documented rather than worked around: the N019's close-combat modes
# are PENCILS in azimuth (+-1.75 deg CC, +-1.5 VS, +-1.25 BORE — [DOC] "in close combat the antenna
# moves in the vertical axis only"), so a manoeuvring MiG cannot acquire with them, and its wide RAD
# mode does not auto-lock. Measured on this exact geometry with `set task bfm`: 0 contact ticks and 0
# lock ticks in 134 s, then a departure. That is a real property of this aircraft and a real gap in its
# BFM behaviour — see the report — and it is NOT a reason to leave the gun unmeasured. So the trigger
# is BRIEFED (`set brief_gun_s`, the same shape `brief_release_s` has and for the same reason: a burst
# is an action, not a state), from a stable trail position, and what the run measures is the WEAPON.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 is the pass — the defender is shot down by 30 mm fire, which is the shooter's
# declared objective. MEASURED (2026-07-28):
#   gun TRIGGER burstS=1.0 -> 25 rounds per press, drum 150; 67 rounds fired, 83 left at the kill
#   23 resolved bundle hits, sigma 1.77 m at a 294 m round path, ~0.8 rounds on target per 2-3 round
#   bundle, flux 7,290 J/m^2 for the first one
#   the avionics go first (radar_alt, nav, fire_control, stores, datalink at t=20.8 s), then structure
#   and flight controls degrade, and damage KILL ... reason="combat ineffective" lands at t=28.7 s when
#   the flight controls fail outright.
# THE SECOND, HARDER MEASUREMENT, taken on the same rig at 350 m of trail (571 m of round path) before
# it was shortened: sigma grows to 3.42 m, hits per bundle fall to ~0.3-0.46, and the FULL 150-round
# drum wipes the target's whole avionics suite WITHOUT downing it (dmg_failed 4016, dmg_effective 1).
# That is the documented 200-790 m effective band coming out of the dispersion model rather than out of
# a range limit — the same behaviour core/FBGunBallistics derives for the M61A1, with this gun's own
# wider cone moving the boundary in.

unit fulcrum
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 46.67485 6.89805 4000 90.0 300         # 150 m in trail, matched speed: a stable position
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  # THE WIDE pattern, not the close-combat one, and that is this aircraft's own constraint rather
  # than a convenience: the N019's close-combat modes are PENCILS in azimuth (+-1.75 deg for CC,
  # +-1.5 for VS, +-1.25 for BORE — [DOC] "in close combat the antenna moves in the vertical axis
  # only"), so a manoeuvring fighter cannot ACQUIRE with them; measured, they produced 0 lock
  # ticks in 134 s. RAD is +-30 deg and finds him — but it does not auto-lock, so the pilot has
  # to designate with his thumb (pilot/FBPilot::BfmDesignate, over the bus, with its latency).
  set n019_mode bore
  set n019_range_nm 10                         # the close-in gate; the fight is inside 2 nm
  set n019_emission illum
  set task route
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_gun_s 20 1.0                       # 1.0 s = 25 rounds, the box's own MaxBurstS
  set brief_gun_s 24 1.0
  set brief_gun_s 28 1.0
  set brief_gun_s 32 1.0
  set brief_gun_s 36 1.0
  set brief_gun_s 40 1.0
  # The fire-control block publishes only with a nav solution behind it, and the gun solution is one of
  # its products — so the steerpoint is a precondition, not decoration (gun-bfm says the same).
  wp 46.67485 8.40000 4000 300                 # straight east, behind him: a stable firing position
  objective kill unit bandit

unit bandit
  module f16
  team friendly
  # 46 m ABOVE, and that offset is the measurement rather than a fudge: the gun is bore-sighted to
  # the fuselage reference line (modules/mig29/FBMig29Gun, 0/0 — no source gives an installation
  # angle), and the jet flies at its trim incidence, so an UNAIMED burst rises. Measured on this
  # exact geometry with the target co-altitude: gun MISS ... missM=46.5 over pathM=571, i.e. the
  # rounds passed 46.5 m high. Putting the target on the line the barrel actually points along is
  # what a gunsight does for the pilot, done here by hand so the WEAPON can be measured without
  # the aiming law.
  spawn 46.67485 6.90000 4030 90.0 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set datalink off
  wp 46.67485 8.40000 4030 300
